{
  "name": "FIIT DOD 2025 Treasure Hunt",
  "description": "Find all 6 MONAD devices hidden in the library! These devices are actively broadcasting Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) signals to advertise their presence. BLE beacons are commonly used in indoor positioning systems, proximity marketing, and asset tracking - they transmit small packets of data that nearby devices can detect and use to determine their approximate location within a building.\n\nYour mission is to locate all 6 MONAD devices scattered throughout the library. When you find each device, scan its QR code to confirm the discovery and proceed to the next one. The data collected during this treasure hunt will be used to study the behavior of WiFi and Bluetooth signals in indoor environments, helping researchers understand signal propagation, interference patterns, and improve indoor navigation systems.",
  "available_from": "2025-12-11T00:00:00Z",
  "available_to": "2025-12-12T23:59:59Z",
  "points": 250,
  "estimated_duration": 3,
